-- title:
--   Two images with almost-everywhere separating restrictions generate F'
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $0$, and let $F$ and $F'$ be fields equipped with $K$-algebra structures that are essentially of finite type over $K$ and satisfy `IsCurveOver K F`, `IsCurveOver K F'`: every nonzero element has a principal divisor of degree $0$, every place has residue field finite over $K$, and the module of Kähler differentials over $K$ is free of rank $1$. Here a place of a field $E$ over $K$ is a valuation subring of $E$ containing $\operatorname{im}(K\to E)$, different from $E$ itself, and a principal ideal ring. Let $\varphi_0,\varphi_1\colon F\to F'$ be $K$-algebra homomorphisms whose underlying ring maps are integral and along which $F'$ is a finite $F$-module (i.e. $F'$ is finite as a module over $F$ via $\varphi_i$). Suppose there is a finite set $S$ of places of $F'$ such that any two places $P,P'$ of $F'$ outside $S$ with $\varphi_0^{-1}(\mathcal O_P)=\varphi_0^{-1}(\mathcal O_{P'})$ and $\varphi_1^{-1}(\mathcal O_P)=\varphi_1^{-1}(\mathcal O_{P'})$ are equal. Then the subfield of $F'$ generated by $\operatorname{range}\varphi_0\cup\operatorname{range}\varphi_1$ is all of $F'$.
--
--   This is the function-field separation criterion: a pair of finite coverings of curves whose fibres jointly separate all but finitely many points induces a birational embedding, so the compositum of the two images is the whole function field. It is used to identify the function field of the quaternionic moduli tower in the Čerednik–Drinfeld setting, and to realise automorphisms of uniformised Hecke curves from orbit-separating data.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Place_subfieldClosure_range_union_eq_top_of_restrictAlong_injOn.lean

